#!/bin/bash

# omarchy:summary=Installing themes from remote git repositories is disabled on Ombuntu
# omarchy:args=[git-repo-url]

cat >&2 <<'MSG'
Ombuntu does not install themes from remote repositories: a theme can carry
executable content (neovim.lua, templates) and would run with your user rights.

Use one of the 19 bundled themes (Super + Ctrl + Shift + Space), or review a
theme yourself and copy it into ~/.config/omarchy/themes/<name>/.
MSG
exit 1
